.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH shx 1  "shx 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
shx \- Print\-only natural\-language to shell\-command translator
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshx\fR [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-why\fR] [\fB\-\-local\fR] [\fB\-\-cloud\fR] [\fB\-\-offline\fR] [\fB\-\-copy\fR] [\fB\-\-exit\-on\-risk\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-memory\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIINTENT\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print\-only natural\-language to shell\-command translator
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-count\fR \fI<N>\fR
Return up to N candidates (one command per stdout line)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Structured JSON object on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR \fI<CMD>\fR
Reverse mode: explain an existing command (T\-601)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
Refine session (T\-602)
.TP
\fB\-\-why\fR
Show which memory entries / routing were used (stderr)
.TP
\fB\-\-local\fR
Force the local backend
.TP
\fB\-\-cloud\fR
Force the cloud backend (error if unconfigured)
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Forbid network; use mock/fixtures
.TP
\fB\-\-copy\fR
Copy the result to the clipboard (T\-603)
.TP
\fB\-\-exit\-on\-risk\fR
Exit 3 if risk ≥ Review
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-memory\fR
Ignore memory for this call
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable ANSI on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Named context profile
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Override project scoping
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip tool\-side prompts (never execution)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Raw model output and full error chains on stderr
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Alternate config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIINTENT\fR]
Natural\-language intent (joined with spaces)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
shx\-doctor(1)
Self\-check config, DB, and backends (T\-007)
.TP
shx\-history(1)
Browse recorded translations (T\-204)
.TP
shx\-snippet(1)
Named command macros (T\-504). Never auto\-run as `shx <name>`
.TP
shx\-teach(1)
Teach shorthand vocabulary (T\-205)
.TP
shx\-feedback(1)
Record feedback on an interaction (T\-503)
.TP
shx\-config(1)
Inspect or edit configuration (T\-007)
.TP
shx\-import\-history(1)
Opt\-in shell\-history ingest (T\-605)
.TP
shx\-completion(1)
Generate shell completions (T\-604)
.TP
shx\-man(1)
Print the man page (T\-604)
.TP
shx\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
stdout is the command only; explanations and warnings go to stderr.
.SH VERSION
v0.0.0
